How a Flattened City Grew Back (被炸平的城市怎样长回来) — Projection on White Model (Lemo-Opuscar) · LemoLab × Claude Opus 5.5

No AI-generated images, no stock footage, no photographs. The model is extruded from open building data in code; every
light, colour, shadow, label and line is drawn by the page (three.js + 2D canvas). Download URLs are in build.sh
(accessed 2026-10-16); the raw files are cached in assets/raw/.

DATA (credited on screen top-left "3DBAG / BAG / BGT" and on the end card)
- 3DBAG, LOD1.3 building parts with roof heights reconstructed from AHN LiDAR, by 3DGI and the 3D geoinformation
  research group, TU Delft. https://3dbag.nl — licence CC BY 4.0. Fetched via the 3DBAG WFS (layer BAG3D:lod13).
  Used: footprints, roof heights (b3_h_70p − b3_h_maaiveld), building identifiers.
- BAG (Basisregistratie Adressen en Gebouwen), Kadaster: original construction year (oorspronkelijkbouwjaar),
  delivered inside the 3DBAG attributes. Licence CC0 1.0.
- BGT (Basisregistratie Grootschalige Topografie), collections "waterdeel" (water) and "overbruggingsdeel" (bridge
  decks), via the PDOK OGC API https://api.pdok.nl/lv/bgt/ogc/v1 — licence CC0 1.0 (stated in the API metadata).
- Modifications: cropped to RD x 91700–94000, y 435300–437900; extruded at 1:1000; shared walls removed; water
  rasterised to a mask; a 2 m heightfield and noon shadow derived (tools/prep.py). The credits above still apply.
- Sun positions computed (NOAA / Meeus solar position algorithm, tools/sun.py); RD ↔ WGS84 by the published
  approximation formulas (tools/rd.py). No external data.

